NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "WARNING: Most of the inner API is not stable yet."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "Here are a few examples of the basic load and dump methods:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "    use YAML::PP;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 "    my $yaml = <<'EOM';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "    --- # Document one is a mapping"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "    name: Tina"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "    age: 29"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "    favourite language: Perl"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 "    --- # Document two is a sequence"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "    - plain string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 "    - 'in single quotes'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "    - \"in double quotes we have escapes! like \\t and \\n\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 "    - | # a literal block scalar"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "      line1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 "      line2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "    - > # a folded block scalar"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 "      this is all one"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 "      single line because the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 "      linebreaks will be folded"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "    EOM"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "    my @documents = $ypp->load_string($yaml);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 "    my @documents = $ypp->load_file($filename);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 "    my $yaml = $ypp->dump_string($data1, $data2);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 "    $ypp->dump_file($filename, $data1, $data2);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 "    # Enable perl data types and objects"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new(schema => [qw/ + Perl /]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 "    my $yaml = $yp->dump_string($data_with_perl_objects);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 "    # Legacy interface"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "    use YAML::PP qw/ Load Dump LoadFile DumpFile /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000450 "    my @documents = Load($yaml);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000451 "    my @documents = LoadFile($filename);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000452 "    my @documents = LoadFile($filehandle);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000453 "    my $yaml = = Dump(@documents);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000454 "    DumpFile($filename, @documents);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000455 "    DumpFile($filenhandle @documents);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000457 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000458 "Some utility scripts, mostly useful for debugging:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000459 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000460 "    # Load YAML into a data structure and dump with Data::Dumper"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000461 "    yamlpp-load < file.yaml"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000462 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000463 "    # Load and Dump"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000464 "    yamlpp-load-dump < file.yaml"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000465 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000466 "    # Print the events from the parser in yaml-test-suite format"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000467 "    yamlpp-events < file.yaml"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000468 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000469 "    # Parse and emit events directly without loading"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000470 "    yamlpp-parse-emit < file.yaml"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000471 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000472 "    # Create ANSI colored YAML. Can also be useful for invalid YAML, showing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000473 "    # you the exact location of the error"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000474 "    yamlpp-highlight < file.yaml"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000475 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000476 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000477 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000478 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000479 "YAML::PP is a modular YAML processor."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000480 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000481 "It aims to support C<YAML 1.2> and C<YAML 1.1>. See L<https://yaml.org/>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000482 "Some (rare) syntax elements are not yet supported and documented below."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000483 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000484 "YAML is a serialization language. The YAML input is called \"YAML Stream\"."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000485 "A stream consists of one or more \"Documents\", separated by a line with a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000486 "document start marker C<--->. A document optionally ends with the document"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000487 "end marker C<...>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000488 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000489 "This allows one to process continuous streams additionally to a fixed input"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000490 "file or string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000491 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000492 "The YAML::PP frontend will currently load all documents, and return only"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000493 "the first if called with scalar context."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000494 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000495 "The YAML backend is implemented in a modular way that allows one to add"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000496 "custom handling of YAML tags, perl objects and data types. The inner API"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000497 "is not yet stable. Suggestions welcome."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000498 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000499 "You can check out all current parse and load results from the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000500 "yaml-test-suite here:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000501 "L<https://perlpunk.github.io/YAML-PP-p5/test-suite.html>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000502 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000503 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000504 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000505 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000506 "=head2 new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000507 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000508 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000509 "    "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000510 "    # use YAML 1.2 Failsafe Schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000511 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( schema => ['Failsafe'] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000512 "    # use YAML 1.2 JSON Schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000513 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( schema => ['JSON'] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000514 "    # use YAML 1.2 Core Schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000515 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( schema => ['Core'] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000516 "    "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000517 "    # Die when detecting cyclic references"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000518 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( cyclic_refs => 'fatal' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000519 "    "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000520 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000521 "        boolean => 'perl',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000522 "        schema => ['Core'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000523 "        cyclic_refs => 'fatal',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000524 "        indent => 4,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000525 "        header => 1,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000526 "        footer => 0,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000527 "        version_directive => 0,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000528 "        require_footer => 0,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000529 "        max_depth => 512,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000530 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000532 "Options:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000534 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000535 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000536 "=item boolean"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000537 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000538 "Values: C<perl> (currently default), C<JSON::PP>, C<boolean>, C<perl_experimental>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000540 "This option is for loading and dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000541 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000542 "In case of perl 5.36 and later, builtin booleans should work out of the box"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000543 "(since YAML::PP >= 0.38.0)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000544 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000545 "    print YAML::PP->new->dump_string([ builtin::true, !1 ]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000546 "    # ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000547 "    # - true"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000548 "    # - false"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000549 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000550 "For earlier perl versions, you can use \"pseudo\" booleans like documented"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000551 "in the following examples."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000552 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000553 "    # load/dump booleans via boolean.pm"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000554 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( boolean => 'boolean' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000555 "    # load/dump booleans via JSON::PP::true/false"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000556 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new( boolean => 'JSON::PP' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000557 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000558 "You can also specify more than one class, comma separated."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000559 "This is important for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000560 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000561 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000562 "    boolean => 'JSON::PP,boolean'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000563 "    Booleans will be loaded as JSON::PP::Booleans, but when dumping, also"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000564 "    'boolean' objects will be recognized"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000565 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000566 "    boolean => 'JSON::PP,*'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000567 "    Booleans will be loaded as JSON::PP::Booleans, but when dumping, all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000568 "    currently supported boolean classes will be recognized"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000569 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000570 "    boolean => '*'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000571 "    Booleans will be loaded as perl booleans, but when dumping, all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000572 "    currently supported boolean classes will be recognized"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000574 "    boolean => ''"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000575 "    Booleans will be loaded as perl booleans, but when dumping, nothing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000576 "    will be recognized as booleans."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000577 "    This option is for backwards compatibility for perl versions < 5.36,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000578 "    if you rely on [!!1, !1] being dumped as [1, '']."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000579 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000580 "The option C<perl_experimental> was introduced when experimental boolean"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000581 "support was added to perl 5.36. Since it will not be experimental anymore"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000582 "in perl 5.40 \\o/ the option is deprecated and the same as C<perl>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000583 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000584 "=item schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000585 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000586 "Default: C<['Core']>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000587 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000588 "This option is for loading and dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000589 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000590 "Array reference. Here you can define what schema to use."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000591 "Supported standard Schemas are: C<Failsafe>, C<JSON>, C<Core>, C<YAML1_1>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000593 "To get an overview how the different Schemas behave, see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000594 "L<https://perlpunk.github.io/YAML-PP-p5/schemas.html>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000595 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000596 "Additionally you can add further schemas, for example C<Merge>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000597 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000598 "=item cyclic_refs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000599 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000600 "Default: C<fatal> (since 0.037)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000601 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000602 "Before the default was C<allow>, but this can lead to memory leaks"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000603 "when loading on untrusted data, so it was changed to C<fatal> by default."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000604 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000605 "This option is for loading only."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000606 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000607 "Defines what to do when a cyclic reference is detected when loading."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000608 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000609 "    # fatal  - die"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000610 "    # warn   - Just warn about them and replace with undef"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000611 "    # ignore - replace with undef"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000612 "    # allow  - Default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000613 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000614 "=item duplicate_keys"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000615 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000616 "Default: 0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000617 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000618 "Since version 0.027"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000619 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000620 "This option is for loading."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000621 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000622 "The YAML Spec says duplicate mapping keys should be forbidden."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000623 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000624 "When set to true, duplicate keys in mappings are allowed (and will overwrite"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000625 "the previous key)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000626 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000627 "When set to false, duplicate keys will result in an error when loading."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000628 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000629 "This is especially useful when you have a longer mapping and don't see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000630 "the duplicate key in your editor:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000631 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000632 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000633 "    a: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000634 "    b: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000635 "    # ............."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000636 "    a: 23 # error"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000637 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000638 "=item indent"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000639 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000640 "Default: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000641 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000642 "This option is for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000643 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000644 "Use that many spaces for indenting"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000645 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000646 "=item width"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000648 "Since version 0.025"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000650 "Default: 80"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000651 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000652 "This option is for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000653 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000654 "Maximum columns when dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000655 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000656 "This is only respected when dumping flow collections right now."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000658 "in the future it will be used also for wrapping long strings."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000659 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000660 "=item header"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000661 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000662 "Default: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000663 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000664 "This option is for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000665 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000666 "Print document header C<--->"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000667 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000668 "=item footer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000669 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000670 "Default: 0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000671 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000672 "Since version v0.39"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000673 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000674 "This option is for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000675 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000676 "Print document footer C<...>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000678 "=item require_footer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000679 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000680 "Default: 0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000681 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000682 "Will require a C<...> at the end of each document."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000683 "This can be useful in a context where you want to make sure you received"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000684 "the complete content, for example over network."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000685 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000686 "    # Good"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000687 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000688 "    a: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000689 "    ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000690 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000691 "    a: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000692 "    ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000693 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000694 "    # Bad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000695 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000696 "    a: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000697 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000698 "    a: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000699 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000700 "=item max_depth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000701 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000702 "Since version v0.40"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000703 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000704 "default: 512"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000705 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000706 "Loading deeply nested, but still small YAML documents, like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000707 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000708 "    [[[[[[[[[[...]]]]]]]]]]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000709 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000710 "can be significantly slower than a \"normal\" document with the same size."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000711 "By default the depth is limited to 512, which should be more than enough"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000712 "for 99% of the use cases."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000713 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000714 "=item yaml_version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000715 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000716 "Since version 0.020"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000717 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000718 "This option is for loading and dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000719 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000720 "Default: C<1.2>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000721 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000722 "Note that in this case, a directive C<%YAML 1.1> will basically be ignored"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000723 "and everything loaded with the C<1.2 Core> Schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000724 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000725 "If you want to support both YAML 1.1 and 1.2, you have to specify that, and the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000726 "schema (C<Core> or C<YAML1_1>) will be chosen automatically."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000727 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000728 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000729 "        yaml_version => ['1.2', '1.1'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000730 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000731 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000732 "This is the same as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000733 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000734 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000735 "        schema => ['+'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000736 "        yaml_version => ['1.2', '1.1'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000737 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000738 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000739 "because the C<+> stands for the default schema per version."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000740 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000741 "When loading, and there is no C<%YAML> directive, C<1.2> will be considered"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000742 "as default, and the C<Core> schema will be used."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000743 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000744 "If there is a C<%YAML 1.1> directive, the C<YAML1_1> schema will be used."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000745 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000746 "Of course, you can also make C<1.1> the default:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000747 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000748 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000749 "        yaml_version => ['1.1', '1.2'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000750 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000751 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000752 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000753 "You can also specify C<1.1> only:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000754 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000755 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000756 "        yaml_version => ['1.1'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000757 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000758 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000759 "In this case also documents with C<%YAML 1.2> will be loaded with the C<YAML1_1>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000760 "schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000761 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000762 "=item version_directive"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000763 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000764 "Since version 0.020"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000765 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000766 "This option is for dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000767 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000768 "Default: 0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000769 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000770 "Print Version Directive C<%YAML 1.2> (or C<%YAML 1.1>) on top of each YAML"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000771 "document. It will use the first version specified in the C<yaml_version> option."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000772 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000773 "=item preserve"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000774 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000775 "Since version 0.021"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000776 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000777 "Default: false"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000778 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000779 "This option is for loading and dumping."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000780 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000781 "Preserving scalar styles is still experimental."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000782 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000783 "    use YAML::PP::Common qw/ :PRESERVE /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000784 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000785 "    # Preserve the order of hash keys"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000786 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new( preserve => PRESERVE_ORDER );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000787 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000788 "    # Preserve the quoting style of scalars"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000789 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new( preserve => PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000790 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000791 "    # Preserve block/flow style (since 0.024)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000792 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new( preserve => PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000793 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000794 "    # Preserve alias names (since 0.027)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000795 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new( preserve => PRESERVE_ALIAS );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000796 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000797 "    # Combine, e.g. preserve order and scalar style"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000798 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new( preserve => PRESERVE_ORDER | PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000799 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000800 "Do NOT rely on the internal implementation of it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000801 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000802 "If you load the following input:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000803 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000804 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000805 "    z: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000806 "    a: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000807 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000808 "    - plain"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000809 "    - 'single'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000810 "    - \"double\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000811 "    - |"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000812 "      literal"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000813 "    - >"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000814 "      folded"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000815 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000816 "    block mapping: &alias"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000817 "      flow sequence: [a, b]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000818 "    same mapping: *alias"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000819 "    flow mapping: {a: b}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000820 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000821 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000822 "with this code:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000823 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000824 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000825 "        preserve => PRESERVE_ORDER | PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000826 "                    | PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE | PRESERVE_ALIAS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000827 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000828 "    my ($hash, $styles, $flow) = $yp->load_file($file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000829 "    $yp->dump_file($hash, $styles, $flow);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000830 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000831 "Then dumping it will return the same output."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000832 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000833 "Note that YAML allows repeated definition of anchors. They cannot be preserved"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000834 "with YAML::PP right now. Example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000835 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000836 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000837 "    - &seq [a]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000838 "    - *seq"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000839 "    - &seq [b]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000840 "    - *seq"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000841 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000842 "Because the data could be shuffled before dumping again, the anchor definition"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000843 "could be broken. In this case repeated anchor names will be discarded when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000844 "loading and dumped with numeric anchors like usual."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000845 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000846 "Implementation:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000847 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000848 "When loading, hashes will be tied to an internal class"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000849 "(C<YAML::PP::Preserve::Hash>) that keeps the key order."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000850 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000851 "Scalars will be returned as objects of an internal class"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000852 "(C<YAML::PP::Preserve::Scalar>) with overloading. If you assign to such"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000853 "a scalar, the object will be replaced by a simple scalar."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000854 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000855 "    # assignment, style gets lost"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000856 "    $styles->[1] .= ' append';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000857 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000858 "You can also pass C<1> as a value. In this case all preserving options will be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000859 "enabled, also if there are new options added in the future."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000860 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000861 "There are also methods to create preserved nodes from scratch. See the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000862 "C<preserved_(scalar|mapping|sequence)> L<\"METHODS\"> below."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000863 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000864 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000865 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000866 "=head2 load_string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000867 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000868 "    my $doc = $ypp->load_string(\"foo: bar\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000869 "    my @docs = $ypp->load_string(\"foo: bar\\n---\\n- a\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000870 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000871 "Input should be Unicode characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000872 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000873 "So if you read from a file, you should decode it, for example with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000874 "C<Encode::decode()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000875 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000876 "Note that in scalar context, C<load_string> and C<load_file> return the first"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000877 "document (like L<YAML::Syck>), while L<YAML> and L<YAML::XS> return the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000878 "last."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000879 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000880 "=head2 load_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000881 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000882 "    my $doc = $ypp->load_file(\"file.yaml\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000883 "    my @docs = $ypp->load_file(\"file.yaml\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000884 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000885 "Strings will be loaded as unicode characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000886 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000887 "=head2 dump_string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000888 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000889 "    my $yaml = $ypp->dump_string($doc);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000890 "    my $yaml = $ypp->dump_string($doc1, $doc2);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000891 "    my $yaml = $ypp->dump_string(@docs);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000892 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000893 "Input strings should be Unicode characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000894 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000895 "Output will return Unicode characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000896 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000897 "So if you want to write that to a file (or pass to YAML::XS, for example),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000898 "you typically encode it via C<Encode::encode()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000899 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000900 "=head2 dump_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000901 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000902 "    $ypp->dump_file(\"file.yaml\", $doc);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000903 "    $ypp->dump_file(\"file.yaml\", $doc1, $doc2);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000904 "    $ypp->dump_file(\"file.yaml\", @docs);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000905 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000906 "Input data should be Unicode characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000907 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000908 "=head2 dump"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000909 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000910 "This will dump to a predefined writer. By default it will just use the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000911 "L<YAML::PP::Writer> and output a string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000912 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000913 "    my $writer = MyWriter->new(\\my $output);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000914 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000915 "        writer => $writer,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000916 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000917 "    $yp->dump($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000918 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000919 "=head2 preserved_scalar"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000920 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000921 "Since version 0.024"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000922 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000923 "Experimental. Please report bugs or let me know this is useful and works."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000924 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000925 "You can define a certain scalar style when dumping data."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000926 "Figuring out the best style is a hard task and practically impossible to get"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000927 "it right for all cases. It's also a matter of taste."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000928 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000929 "    use YAML::PP::Common qw/ PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE YAML_LITERAL_SCALAR_STYLE /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000930 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000931 "        preserve => PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000932 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000933 "    # a single linebreak would normally be dumped with double quotes: \"\\n\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000934 "    my $scalar = $yp->preserved_scalar(\"\\n\", style => YAML_LITERAL_SCALAR_STYLE );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000935 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000936 "    my $data = { literal => $scalar };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000937 "    my $dump = $yp->dump_string($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000938 "    # output"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000939 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000940 "    literal: |+"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000941 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000942 "    ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000943 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000944 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000945 "=head2 preserved_mapping, preserved_sequence"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000946 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000947 "Since version 0.024"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000948 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000949 "Experimental. Please report bugs or let me know this is useful and works."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000950 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000951 "With this you can define which nodes are dumped with the more compact flow"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000952 "style instead of block style."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000953 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000954 "If you add C<PRESERVE_ORDER> to the C<preserve> option, it will also keep the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000955 "order of the keys in a hash."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000956 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000957 "    use YAML::PP::Common qw/"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000958 "        PRESERVE_ORDER PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000959 "        YAML_FLOW_MAPPING_STYLE YAML_FLOW_SEQUENCE_STYLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000960 "    /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000961 "    my $yp = YAML::PP->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000962 "        preserve => PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE | PRESERVE_ORDER"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000963 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000964 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000965 "    my $hash = $yp->preserved_mapping({}, style => YAML_FLOW_MAPPING_STYLE);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000966 "    # Add values after initialization to preserve order"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000967 "    %$hash = (z => 1, a => 2, y => 3, b => 4);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000968 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000969 "    my $array = $yp->preserved_sequence([23, 24], style => YAML_FLOW_SEQUENCE_STYLE);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000970 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000971 "    my $data = $yp->preserved_mapping({});"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000972 "    %$data = ( map => $hash, seq => $array );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000973 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000974 "    my $dump = $yp->dump_string($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000975 "    # output"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000976 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000977 "    map: {z: 1, a: 2, y: 3, b: 4}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000978 "    seq: [23, 24]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000979 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000980 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000981 "=head2 loader"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000982 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000983 "Returns or sets the loader object, by default L<YAML::PP::Loader>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000984 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000985 "=head2 dumper"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000986 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000987 "Returns or sets the dumper object, by default L<YAML::PP::Dumper>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000988 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000989 "=head2 schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000990 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000991 "Returns or sets the schema object"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000992 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000993 "=head2 default_schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000994 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000995 "Creates and returns the default schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000996 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000997 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000998 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000999 "The functions C<Load>, C<LoadFile>, C<Dump> and C<DumpFile> are provided"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001000 "as a drop-in replacement for other existing YAML processors."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001001 "No function is exported by default."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001002 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001003 "Note that in scalar context, C<Load> and C<LoadFile> return the first"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001004 "document (like L<YAML::Syck>), while L<YAML> and L<YAML::XS> return the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001005 "last."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001006 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001007 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001008 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001009 "=item Load"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001010 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001011 "    use YAML::PP qw/ Load /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001012 "    my $doc = Load($yaml);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001013 "    my @docs = Load($yaml);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001014 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001015 "Works like C<load_string>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001016 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001017 "=item LoadFile"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001018 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001019 "    use YAML::PP qw/ LoadFile /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001020 "    my $doc = LoadFile($file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001021 "    my @docs = LoadFile($file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001022 "    my @docs = LoadFile($filehandle);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001023 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001024 "Works like C<load_file>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001025 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001026 "=item Dump"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001027 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001028 "    use YAML::PP qw/ Dump /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001029 "    my $yaml = Dump($doc);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001030 "    my $yaml = Dump(@docs);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001031 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001032 "Works like C<dump_string>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001033 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001034 "=item DumpFile"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001036 "    use YAML::PP qw/ DumpFile /;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001037 "    DumpFile($file, $doc);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001038 "    DumpFile($file, @docs);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001039 "    DumpFile($filehandle, @docs);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001040 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001041 "Works like C<dump_file>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001043 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001044 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001045 "=head1 PLUGINS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001046 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001047 "You can alter the behaviour of YAML::PP by using the following schema"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001048 "classes:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001049 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001050 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001051 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001052 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Failsafe>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001054 "One of the three YAML 1.2 official schemas"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001055 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001056 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::JSON>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001057 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001058 "One of the three YAML 1.2 official schemas."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001059 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001060 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Core>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001061 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001062 "One of the three YAML 1.2 official schemas. Default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001063 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001064 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::YAML1_1>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001065 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001066 "Schema implementing the most common YAML 1.1 types"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001068 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Perl>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001069 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001070 "Serializing Perl objects and types"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001071 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001072 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Binary>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001073 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001074 "Serializing binary data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001075 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001076 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Merge>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001077 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001078 "YAML 1.1 merge keys for mappings"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001079 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001080 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Catchall>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001082 "Experimental."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001083 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001084 "It was accidentally added in 0.38.1, and unknown tags forbidden."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001085 "This was reverted in 0.39.0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001086 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001087 "By default they will result in an error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001088 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001089 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Include>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001090 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001091 "Include other YAML files via C<!include> tags"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001092 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001093 "=item L<YAML::PP::Schema::Tie::IxHash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001094 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001095 "Deprecated. See option C<preserve>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001096 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001097 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001098 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001099 "To make the parsing process faster, you can plugin the libyaml parser"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001100 "with L<YAML::PP::LibYAML>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001101 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001102 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001104 "=head1 IMPLEMENTATION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001105 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001106 "The process of loading and dumping is split into the following steps:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001107 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001108 "    Load:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001109 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001110 "    YAML Stream        Tokens        Event List        Data Structure"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001111 "              --------->    --------->        --------->"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001112 "                lex           parse           construct"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001113 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001114 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001115 "    Dump:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001116 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001117 "    Data Structure       Event List        YAML Stream"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001118 "                --------->        --------->"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001119 "                represent           emit"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001120 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001122 "You can dump basic perl types like hashes, arrays, scalars (strings, numbers)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001123 "For dumping blessed objects and things like coderefs have a look at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001124 "L<YAML::PP::Perl>/L<YAML::PP::Schema::Perl>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001125 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001126 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001127 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001128 "=item L<YAML::PP::Lexer>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001129 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001130 "The Lexer is reading the YAML stream into tokens. This makes it possible"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001131 "to generate syntax highlighted YAML output."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001133 "Note that the API to retrieve the tokens will change."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001134 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001135 "=item L<YAML::PP::Parser>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001136 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001137 "The Parser retrieves the tokens from the Lexer. The main YAML content is then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001138 "parsed with the Grammar."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001139 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001140 "=item L<YAML::PP::Grammar>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001141 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001142 "=item L<YAML::PP::Constructor>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001143 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001144 "The Constructor creates a data structure from the Parser events."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001145 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001146 "=item L<YAML::PP::Loader>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001147 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001148 "The Loader combines the constructor and parser."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001149 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001150 "=item L<YAML::PP::Dumper>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001151 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001152 "The Dumper will delegate to the Representer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001153 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001154 "=item L<YAML::PP::Representer>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001155 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001156 "The Representer will create Emitter events from the given data structure."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001157 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001158 "=item L<YAML::PP::Emitter>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001159 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001160 "The Emitter creates a YAML stream."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001161 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001162 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001163 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001164 "=head2 YAML::PP::Parser"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001165 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001166 "Still TODO:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001167 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001168 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001169 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001170 "=item Implicit collection keys"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001171 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001172 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001173 "    [ a, b, c ]: value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001175 "=item Implicit mapping in flow style sequences"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001176 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001177 "This is supported since 0.029 (except some not relevant cases):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001178 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001179 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001180 "    [ a, b, c: d ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001181 "    # equals"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001182 "    [ a, b, { c: d } ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001183 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001184 "=item Plain mapping keys ending with colons"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001185 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001186 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001187 "    key ends with two colons::: value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001188 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001189 "This was implemented in 0.037."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001190 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001191 "=item Supported Characters"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001192 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001193 "If you have valid YAML that's not parsed, or the other way round, please"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001194 "create an issue."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001195 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001196 "=item Line and Column Numbers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001197 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001198 "You will see line and column numbers in the error message. The column numbers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001199 "might still be wrong in some cases."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001200 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001201 "=item Error Messages"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001203 "The error messages need to be improved."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001204 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001205 "=item Unicode Surrogate Pairs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001206 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001207 "Currently loaded as single characters without validating"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001208 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001209 "=item Possibly more"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001210 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001211 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001212 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001213 "=head2 YAML::PP::Constructor"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001214 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001215 "The Constructor now supports all three YAML 1.2 Schemas, Failsafe, JSON and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001216 "Core.  Additionally you can choose the schema for YAML 1.1 as C<YAML1_1>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001217 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001218 "Too see what strings are resolved as booleans, numbers, null etc. look at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001219 "L<https://perlpunk.github.io/YAML-PP-p5/schema-examples.html>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001220 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001221 "You can choose the Schema like this:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001222 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001223 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new(schema => ['JSON']); # default is 'Core'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001224 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001225 "The Tags C<!!seq> and C<!!map> are still ignored for now."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001226 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001227 "It supports:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001228 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001229 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001230 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001231 "=item Handling of Anchors/Aliases"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001232 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001233 "Like in modules like L<YAML>, the Constructor will use references for mappings and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001234 "sequences, but obviously not for scalars."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001235 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001236 "L<YAML::XS> uses real aliases, which allows also aliasing scalars. I might add"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001237 "an option for that since aliasing is now available in pure perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001238 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001239 "=item Boolean Handling"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001240 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001241 "You can choose between C<'perl'> (1/'', currently default), C<'JSON::PP'> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001242 "C<'boolean'>.pm for handling boolean types.  That allows you to dump the data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001243 "structure with one of the JSON modules without losing information about"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001244 "booleans."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001245 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001246 "=item Numbers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001247 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001248 "Numbers are created as real numbers instead of strings, so that they are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001249 "dumped correctly by modules like L<JSON::PP> or L<JSON::XS>, for example."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001250 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001251 "=item Complex Keys"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001253 "Mapping Keys in YAML can be more than just scalars. Of course, you can't load"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001254 "that into a native perl structure. The Constructor will stringify those keys"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001255 "with L<Data::Dumper> instead of just returning something like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001256 "C<HASH(0x55dc1b5d0178)>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001257 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001258 "Example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001259 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001260 "    use YAML::PP;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001261 "    use JSON::PP;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001262 "    my $ypp = YAML::PP->new;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001263 "    my $coder = JSON::PP->new->ascii->pretty->allow_nonref->canonical;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001264 "    my $yaml = <<'EOM';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001265 "    complex:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001266 "        ?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001267 "            ?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001268 "                a: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001269 "                c: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001270 "            : 23"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001271 "        : 42"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001272 "    EOM"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001273 "    my $data = $yppl->load_string($yaml);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001274 "    say $coder->encode($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001275 "    __END__"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001276 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001277 "       \"complex\" : {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001278 "          \"{'{a => 1,c => 2}' => 23}\" : 42"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001279 "       }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001280 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001281 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001282 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001283 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001284 "TODO:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001285 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001286 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001287 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001288 "=item Parse Tree"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001289 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001290 "I would like to generate a complete parse tree, that allows you to manipulate"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001291 "the data structure and also dump it, including all whitespaces and comments."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001292 "The spec says that this is throwaway content, but I read that many people"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001293 "wish to be able to keep the comments."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001294 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001295 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001296 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001297 "=head2 YAML::PP::Dumper, YAML::PP::Emitter"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001298 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001299 "The Dumper should be able to dump strings correctly, adding quotes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001300 "whenever a plain scalar would look like a special string, like C<true>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001301 "or when it contains or starts with characters that are not allowed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001302 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001303 "Most strings will be dumped as plain scalars without quotes. If they"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001304 "contain special characters or have a special meaning, they will be dumped"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001305 "with single quotes. If they contain control characters, including <\"\\n\">,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001306 "they will be dumped with double quotes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001307 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001308 "It will recognize JSON::PP::Boolean and boolean.pm objects and dump them"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001309 "correctly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001310 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001311 "Numbers which also have a C<PV> flag will be recognized as numbers and not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001312 "as strings:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001313 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001314 "    my $int = 23;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001315 "    say \"int: $int\"; # $int will now also have a PV flag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001316 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001317 "That means that if you accidentally use a string in numeric context, it will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001318 "also be recognized as a number:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001319 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001320 "    my $string = \"23\";"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001321 "    my $something = $string + 0;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001322 "    print $yp->dump_string($string);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001323 "    # will be emitted as an integer without quotes!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001324 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001325 "The layout is like libyaml output:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001326 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001327 "    key:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001328 "    - a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001329 "    - b"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001330 "    - c"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001331 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001332 "    - key1: 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001333 "      key2: 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001334 "      key3: 3"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001335 "    ---"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001336 "    - - a1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001337 "      - a2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001338 "    - - b1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001339 "      - b2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001340 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001341 "=head1 FAQ - Frequently Asked Questions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001343 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001344 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001345 "=item Are C<<<> merge keys supported?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001346 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001347 "Yes, this can be enabled optionally, see L<YAML::PP::Schema::Merge>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001348 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001349 "=item Is there a linter / formatter for YAML"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001350 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001351 "There is the widely used L<\"yamllint\"|https://yamllint.readthedocs.io/>, based on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001352 "python's PyYAML. It is very configurable and will report errors or warnings."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001353 "It cannot format."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001354 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001355 "Now there is also L<YAML::Tidy>, which will format the given file according"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001356 "to your configuration. So far only a few configuration options exist, but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001357 "they can already be quite helpful."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001359 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001360 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001361 "=head1 Which YAML module should I use?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001362 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001363 "There are many YAML modules on CPAN. For historical reasons some of them"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001364 "aren't handling YAML correctly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001365 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001366 "Most of them are not compatible with the YAML spec and with each other, meaning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001367 "they can interpret the same YAML differently."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001369 "The behaviours we are discussing here can be divided into parsing issues"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001370 "(syntax) and loading/constructing issues (for example type resolving which"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001371 "decides what is a number, boolean or null)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001373 "See also L<https://matrix.yaml.info/> (parsing) and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001374 "L<https://perlpunk.github.io/YAML-PP-p5/schema-examples.html> (loading)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001375 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001376 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001378 "=item L<\"YAML.pm\"|YAML>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001379 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001380 "It was written even before the YAML 1.0 spec was finished and by that enabled"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001381 "perl users to process YAML very early. It might work for you if you have simple"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001382 "data, but it's missing quite some features and can also produce YAML that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001383 "doesn't roundtrip. Nowadays it might be a good idea to switch."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001384 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001385 "=item L<YAML::XS>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001386 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001387 "A libyaml binding that is robust and widely used. However, there are two"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001388 "things to consider."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001389 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001390 "1. (syntax) libyaml diverged from the spec in several aspects. They are rare though."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001391 "2. The type resolving does not adhere to YAML 1.1 or YAML 1.2, meaning it is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001392 "   incompatible with other YAML libraries in perl or other languages."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001393 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001394 "=item L<YAML::Tiny>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001395 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001396 "It implements both a tiny subset of YAML, but also a superset. Meaning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001397 "it will happily accept some YAML documents that are not officially valid."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001398 "Type resolving is also not implemented according to the spec."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001399 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001400 "=item L<YAML::Syck>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001401 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001402 "A binding to libsyck. It is even less compatible to YAML than libyaml. Also"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001403 "type resolving is not implemented according to the spec."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001404 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001405 "=item L<YAML::PP>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001406 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001407 "Regarding YAML syntax, it is the second most YAML 1.2 compatible perl module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001408 "The cases it cannot (yet) parse are not relevant in perl programming,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001409 "e.g. hash keys that are not strings."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001410 "Regarding type resolving, it is compatible with the YAML 1.2 Core schema,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001411 "so it should be possible to exchange data as YAML with other libraries"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001412 "in other languages."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001413 "One downside is that it is the slowest perl YAML module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001414 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001415 "=item L<YAML::Parser>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001416 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001417 "This is a parser generated by the YAML grammar, and it's passing all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001418 "official tests. A L<YAML::PP::Ref> frontend exists that you can use just like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001419 "YAML::PP."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001420 "It is quite slow (although it might be ok for small files depending on the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001421 "use case)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001422 "The error messages it creates on invalid YAML are not helpful currently."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001423 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001424 "=item L<YAML::PP::LibYAML>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001425 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001426 "This combines the L<YAML::LibYAML::API> binding for parsing with the YAML::PP"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001427 "frontend for loading and type resolving."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001428 "It is faster than YAML::PP but slower than YAML::XS."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001429 "The divergence from the YAML spec regarding syntax is usually not a problem,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001430 "and at the same time you have the advantage of being compatible to the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001431 "YAML 1.2 Core Schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001432 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001433 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001435 "=head1 WHY"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001436 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001437 "Why did I start to write a new YAML module?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001438 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001439 "All the available parsers and loaders for Perl are behaving differently,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001440 "and more important, aren't conforming to the spec. L<YAML::XS> is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001441 "doing pretty well, but C<libyaml> only handles YAML 1.1 and diverges"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001442 "a bit from the spec. The pure perl loaders lack support for a number of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001443 "features."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001445 "I was going over L<YAML>.pm issues end of 2016, integrating old patches"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001446 "from rt.cpan.org and creating some pull requests myself. I realized"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001447 "that it would be difficult to patch YAML.pm to parse YAML 1.1 or even 1.2,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001448 "and it would also break existing usages relying on the current behaviour."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001449 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001450 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001451 "In 2016 Ingy döt Net initiated two really cool projects:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001452 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001453 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001454 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001455 "=item L<\"YAML TEST SUITE\">"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001457 "=item L<\"YAML EDITOR\">"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001458 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001459 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001460 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001461 "These projects are a big help for any developer. So I got the idea"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001462 "to write my own parser and started on New Year's Day 2017."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001463 "Without the test suite and the editor I would have never started this."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001464 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001465 "I also started another YAML Test project which allows one to get a quick"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001466 "overview of which frameworks support which YAML features:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001467 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001468 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001469 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001470 "=item L<\"YAML TEST MATRIX\">"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001471 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001472 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001473 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001474 "=head2 YAML TEST SUITE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001475 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001476 "L<https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-suite>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001477 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001478 "It contains almost 400 test cases and expected parsing events and more."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001479 "There will be more tests coming. This test suite allows you to write parsers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001480 "without turning the examples from the Specification into tests yourself."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001481 "Also the examples aren't completely covering all cases - the test suite"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001482 "aims to do that."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001483 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001484 "Thanks also to Felix Krause, who is writing a YAML parser in Nim."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001485 "He turned all the spec examples into test cases."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001486 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001487 "=head2 YAML EDITOR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001488 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001489 "This is a tool to play around with several YAML parsers and loaders in vim."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001490 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001491 "L<https://github.com/yaml/yaml-editor>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001492 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001493 "The project contains the code to build the frameworks (16 as of this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001494 "writing) and put it into one big Docker image."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001495 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001496 "It also contains the yaml-editor itself, which will start a vim in the docker"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001497 "container. It uses a lot of funky vimscript that makes playing with it easy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001498 "and useful. You can choose which frameworks you want to test and see the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001499 "output in a grid of vim windows."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001500 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001501 "Especially when writing a parser it is extremely helpful to have all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001502 "the test cases and be able to play around with your own examples to see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001503 "how they are handled."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001504 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001505 "=head2 YAML TEST MATRIX"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001506 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001507 "I was curious to see how the different frameworks handle the test cases,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001508 "so, using the test suite and the docker image, I wrote some code that runs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001509 "the tests, manipulates the output to compare it with the expected output,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001510 "and created a matrix view."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001511 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001512 "L<https://github.com/perlpunk/yaml-test-matrix>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001513 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001514 "You can find the latest build at L<https://matrix.yaml.info>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001515 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001516 "=head1 CONTRIBUTORS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001517 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001518 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001519 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001520 "=item Ingy döt Net"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001521 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001522 "Ingy is one of the creators of YAML. In 2016 he started the YAML Test Suite"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001523 "and the YAML Editor. He also made useful suggestions on the class"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001524 "hierarchy of YAML::PP."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001526 "=item Felix \"flyx\" Krause"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001528 "Felix answered countless questions about the YAML Specification."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001530 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001532 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001534 "=over"
